{
 "_intentional_changes": "Milestone 2 (2026-11-24): file objects no longer contain \"hash\" (the blob id) in any public response (GET /files/<vanity>, the file list, uploads, PATCH), because it revealed when two links share content, private files included (PLAN.md hardening). Only the internal lookup (and staff tools) expose the storage key. That one field was removed from these responses, which are otherwise byte-identical: file_get, file_get_again, file_get_with_extension, file_get_other_ip, file_get_multi_segment, file_get_no_extension, file_get_anonymous, file_get_bot_owner, file_get_unicode, files_list_after, files_list_alice, files_list_before, files_list_fingerprint, files_list_limit, files_list_limit_json_body, files_list_mimetype, files_list_type. Every other golden response is byte-identical to the Flask capture.",
